        "Solid compression/parallel plate geometries",
        "Axial testing / DMA software module"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "The Instron 5967 universal testing system (EQ15) is the primary instrument for determining compressive stiffness via standard uniaxial compression testing. If your scaffold is very soft or compliant, the Discovery HR20 hybrid rheometer (EQ21) can also measure compressive behavior using its normal force sensor. You will need to confirm with the facility that compression platens and a load cell matched to your scaffold's expected force range are available."
